WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
In Stamps, choose Create stamp.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.300
Name the stamp and set the stamp boundary size.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.300
Choose Image to add a graphic element to the stamp.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:16.000
Select the approval artwork in the file picker and open it.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Position the image inside the stamp boundary.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Add dynamic text and choose the identity field it should display.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.500
Enter prefix text and adjust the dynamic field's size and position.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:38.500
Add more stamp text and arrange the elements inside the boundary.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.500
Adjust the text styling, then choose Save stamp.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.000
The saved stamp appears in the Stamps library.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Select the stamp and click the current PDF page to place it.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The completed stamp is frozen on the PDF at the chosen position.
